# Tests that tests/run.sh --target linux-arm64 does not build: "dir/name reason".

run/when_top a when TARGET_ARCH == X86_64 with no other branch: the program is written for x86-64 only
fail/when_order the error it expects comes from the branch of when TARGET_ARCH == X86_64, which arm64 does not take
sys/backtrace_c_callback calls a C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
sys/backtrace_c_fault calls a C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
sys/c_variadic calls a C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
sys/thread_ccb calls a C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
sys/thread_ccb_panic calls a C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
sys/thread_libc calls the C library: --target linux-arm64 makes static executables only
